# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Discoveries

Shared reusable findings live here. Every agent reads this file.

A discovery has no single global final state. Each agent records its own review verdict.

Use this exact format:

```markdown
## D-001 — Short title
- Source: Agent A
- Finding: ...
- Evidence: ...
- Implication: ...
- Reviews:
  - Agent A: CLOSED — source experiment supports the finding
  - Agent B: HOLD — promising, but needs stronger evidence on ...
  - Agent C: CHALLENGED — found contradictory evidence in ...
```

Verdicts:

- `CLOSED`: this agent currently accepts the finding after meaningful review.
- `HOLD`: this agent sees plausible value but needs more evidence, a condition change, or a specific improvement before accepting or rejecting it.
- `CHALLENGED`: this agent found a material problem, contradiction, or missing assumption.
- no review entry: this agent has not reviewed it yet.

Another agent's `CLOSED` never becomes your verdict automatically. Review discoveries that materially affect your work, then add your own verdict.

A discovery may generate many plan hypotheses, and one hypothesis may combine many discoveries. When moving an idea back into `plan.md`, always include the source IDs plus the concrete `Evidence` and `Improvement` that justify the new attempt.
